+	ret = -EKEYREJECTED;
+	if (v1->ticket_length > AFSTOKEN_RK_TIX_MAX)
+		goto error;
+
	plen = sizeof(*token->kad) + v1->ticket_length;
```
Reason:
The fix adds an explicit check that `v1->ticket_length` does not exceed `AFSTOKEN_RK_TIX_MAX`, the same limit already enforced in the XDR parsing path. If the ticket length is too large, the key preparsing fails with `-EKEYREJECTED`, preventing the oversized token from being accepted and thus avoiding the subsequent `WARN_ON()` in `rxrpc_read()`.

